course: dictionary
lesson: 307
title: Serious words: anaphylaxis
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Anaphylaxis is a very serious word, and the words around it tell you how serious. Context clues are the words and sentences near the hard word. «For a few people a sting causes anaphylaxis, a whole-body allergic reaction: a swollen face or trouble breathing means call 999 at once.» The clues are swollen face, trouble breathing and call 999, so it is an emergency.
explain: Look for the signs in the sentences. Swelling of the face, tongue or throat, wheezing, fainting and hives all show the body is in serious trouble. «Swelling, hives (itchy raised bumps on the skin), coughing or trouble breathing in a person with an allergy may be anaphylaxis: get an adult at once.» The brackets explain hives, so you can read its meaning straight away.
explain: You do not need to panic at the word, but you must act fast. If someone looks unwell after eating or after a sting, tell an adult at once. Use the swap check: put «a sudden, very serious allergic reaction» in place of anaphylaxis, and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Anaphylaxis is a sudden, very serious allergic reaction.
fact: It can make it hard to breathe, and can cause swelling of the face, lips, tongue or throat, a rash, dizziness or fainting.
fact: Anaphylaxis can kill if it is not treated straight away.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «anaphylactic shock» and «anaphylaxis plan».
fact: In an emergency, call the emergency number for your country (such as 999) and use an adrenaline pen if the person has one.
exercise: «Swelling of the face or tongue, wheezing or fainting after a sting is anaphylaxis and an emergency.» What is anaphylaxis? | A type of bee | *A sudden, very serious allergic reaction | A kind of sweet drink | A tiny itch that goes away by itself
exercise: «A few people are so allergic to a bee or wasp sting that their throat can swell and they struggle to breathe.» Find and copy the word that means to get bigger. | *swell | sting | throat | breathe
exercise: What does «hives» mean in «hives (itchy raised bumps on the skin)»? | A kind of bee | A sweet, sticky treat | A loud cough | *Itchy raised bumps on the skin
test: «Anaphylaxis can kill if not treated straight away.» What should you do first if you think someone has anaphylaxis? | Let them sleep it off | Give them a cold drink and wait | *Call the emergency number at once | Wait an hour to see if it passes
test: Which one is a sign of anaphylaxis? | A cold day with grey skies | A full tummy after lunch | *Swelling of the tongue | Laughing with friends
exam: Why does the lesson call anaphylaxis an emergency? | *Because it can quickly make breathing hard and can kill if not treated | Because it always goes away on its own | Because it is only a small itch on the skin | Because it is a fun game played at school
